  "id": "projects-ml#27",
  "source": "projects-ml",
  "title": "Machine learning and analytics projects",
  "section": "Smart car parking: predictive availability system",
  "url": "https://github.com/Data-Fenix/smart-car-parking",
  "text": "Repository: https://github.com/Data-Fenix/smart-car-parking. A machine learning system that predicts parking spot availability per city road segment from historical occupancy, weather and location data. A Random Forest regressor reaches an R2 of 0.916 with a mean absolute error of 1.04 spots and an RMSE of 2.11 spots. The dataset covers 4 months, 57 road segments, more than 1.25 million observations and 13.4 million parking slots tracked between 06:00 and 21:00. Key insights: peak demand on weekdays 10:00 to 15:00 and 18:00 to 21:00; occupancy drops in extreme temperatures (below 7 C or above 30 C) and rain; roads near restaurants, shopping and residential zones show 40%+ higher occupancy; only 25% of segments have public transport access. Features include temporal, weather, location and engineered lag and rolling features. Delivered as a case study notebook, PDF report and presentation.",
  "sentences": [
   "A machine learning system that predicts parking spot availability per city road segment from historical occupancy, weather and location data.",
   "A Random Forest regressor reaches an R2 of 0.916 with a mean absolute error of 1.04 spots and an RMSE of 2.11 spots.",
   "The dataset covers 4 months, 57 road segments, more than 1.25 million observations and 13.4 million parking slots tracked between 06:00 and 21:00.",
   "Key insights: peak demand on weekdays 10:00 to 15:00 and 18:00 to 21:00; occupancy drops in extreme temperatures (below 7 C or above 30 C) and rain; roads near restaurants, shopping and residential zones show 40%+ higher occupancy; only 25% of segments have public transport access.",
   "Features include temporal, weather, location and engineered lag and rolling features.",
   "Delivered as a case study notebook, PDF report and presentation."
  ]
